{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too","id":561899,"title":"Corporations Are People, Too!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-20T07:49:48-07:00","id":561899,"title":"Corporations Are People, Too!","content":"Corporations are people, too, and it's imperative that we end anti-corporate bigotry! If you agree with this sentiment, like this page and share its posts!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/corporationsarepeopletoo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.facebook.com/images/fb_icon_325x325.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/corporationsarepeopletoo\" target=\"_blank\"> Facebook - log in or sign up </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/corporationsarepeopletoo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.facebook.com/corporationsarepeopletoo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Log into Facebook to start sharing and connecting with your friends, family, and people you know. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T09:12:49-07:00","id":561988,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming this is parody. When I thought you might be serious, I was about ready to bite your head off. The notion that corporations are people is one of the most ludicrous and asinine notions I've ever heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T10:54:00-07:00","id":562085,"title":"","content":"Well, strictly speaking, they <i>are </i>people. Masses and masses of people stuck in a cage and filled with messy outlooks and emotions.<br /> <br /> But that's semantics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T11:08:09-07:00","id":562092,"title":"","content":"No, corporations are not people. They're made up of people, but they are not people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T13:16:07-07:00","id":562172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=562092#post562092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, corporations are not people. They're made up of people, but they are not people.</div> </div> </div> </div>B-b-but the government SAYS they're people!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T14:06:31-07:00","id":562193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Macai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=562172#post562172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B-b-but the government SAYS they're people!</div> </div> </div> </div>The average IQ is 100. Roughly half of people are smarter than this, and half are stupider than this. Yet all of these people (with a few exceptions) can vote. Meaning that roughly half of the people who vote for our elected officials have less than average IQ. This does not give me a great deal of confidence in the abilities of the people to choose quality governors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:37:10-07:00","id":562385,"title":"","content":"I'll believe corporations are people when one finally gets arrested for doing something illegal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/457-arcanus-dicere","name":"Arcanus Dicere","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T17:58:07-07:00","id":562417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus Dicere</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=562385#post562385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll believe corporations are people when one finally gets arrested for doing something illegal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you're in luck. A couple years ago, <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2013/01/29/us/louisiana-bp-deal/\" target=\"_blank\">BP pleaded guilty to felony manslaughter charges in Louisiana.</a> And the court really threw the book at them: BP had to pay almost an <i>entire day's earnings</i> in fines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T22:58:52-07:00","id":562670,"title":"","content":"It is pretty interesting how they work. A human-based 'life form' that subsists on money. They've evolved over the years, some are more fit than others, those that weaken get gobbled up by others or die alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T08:52:12-07:00","id":563055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=562193#post562193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The average IQ is 100. Roughly half of people are smarter than this, and half are stupider than this. Yet all of these people (with a few exceptions) can vote. Meaning that roughly half of the people who vote for our elected officials have less than average IQ. This does not give me a great deal of confidence in the abilities of the people to choose quality governors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus the half with above average IQ contains several members with no understanding of human motivations or empathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T18:25:39-07:00","id":563601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=563055#post563055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Plus the half with above average IQ contains several members with no understanding of human motivations or empathy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with this whole line of thought is that it presupposes that voter turnout is the same across IQ deviation groups. Now, I'm both drunk and stoned at the same time, so forgive me if my reading comprehension fails me, but <a href=\"http://anepigone.blogspot.com/2008/09/iq-and-voter-turnout.html\" target=\"_blank\">this blog post</a> seems to suggest that higher IQ correlates to higher likelihood of voting. Now, it is a blog post, but bear in mind that it does cite sources.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that's interesting, at least. Hopefully my inebriation hasn't reduced me to linking to quackery in public. I guess I'll find out soon enough when I sober up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2165-macai","name":"Macai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2165_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:02:14-07:00","id":579455,"title":"","content":"Ah this reminds me of a paper I once read (I think it was research carried out by psychologists) claiming that CEOs and other wealthy upper-managers, are much likelier to be sociopaths. But you know, I'm the crazy one who risks societal prosperity for getting a free undergraduate degree from that pesky welfare state. :P<br /> <br /> Welcome to Cyberpunk Episode 1: So it begins...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T21:52:27-07:00","id":581937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=562092#post562092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, corporations are not people. They're made up of people, but they are not people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure this made sense in your head.<br /> <br /> How can an entity be made up of a given thing and yet not be that thing, at least in part?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T22:19:21-07:00","id":581951,"title":"","content":"In the same way people are not subatomic particles and saying they are even partially that is completely missing a whole lot of context. Do you advocate for the civil rights of subatomic particles or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:22:16-07:00","id":583798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/561899-corporations-are-people-too?p=581951#post581951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the same way people are not subatomic particles and saying they are even partially that is completely missing a whole lot of context. Do you advocate for the civil rights of subatomic particles or something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> It helps that the link is clearly to a madman or a troll. This sort of shit is why I steer clear of facebook, honestly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:01:41-07:00","id":593453,"title":"","content":"The subatomic analogy isn't great, though, as corporations movements are largely decided by people, while subatomic particles don't make decisions (unless I'm well behind on my physics). These decisions are made in a context most people don't really deal with directly, but still ultimately people. Unless you're David Icke, at least. :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T21:15:36-07:00","id":593504,"title":"","content":"Corporations are closer to cults, religious movements or idealogical special interest groups rather than people. The hierarchical structure combined with the sense of responsible &amp; entitlement allows the people within the organization to (rightly or wrongly) rationalize that they aren't responsible for the practices &amp; actions of the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T00:50:54-07:00","id":593622,"title":"","content":"While corporate personhood can easily be mistaken for a straw man argument that extreme capitalism makes countries go crazy (and, honestly, I don't believe it'll hold up very much longer), I like to put a positive spin on it.<br /> <br /> Here we have a world wide precedent that non-biological constructs should be treated as people. This paves the way towards eventual acceptance of AIs, digital consciousnesses, androids, etc. as equal to biological humans. For something that is essentially legalization of oligarchs buying politicians and controlling the political process, it just might turn out that the good from it eventually outweighs the immediate bad.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I feel like corporate human rights are wasted on just applying to buying elections. There's so much untapped potential there it makes my head spin. Let's have two corporations marry. Then let's have them divorce. Let's have someone adopted by corporations. Let's have a corporation adopted by someone. There is no lid on that pot.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Holy cows, I just realized I wrote &quot;scarecrow argument&quot;. What the hell, brain? I really shouldn't be posting before my morning coffee... I meant &quot;straw man argument&quot;, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2050,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","user":"Dawngreeter","date":". 07-17-2015, 06:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2050-dawngreeter","name":"Dawngreeter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2050_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T03:18:28-07:00","id":593678,"title":"","content":"Corporate personhood is both hundreds of years old and not actually meant to treat corporations as people. It is a legal fiction created to simplify the business of dealing with corporations, namely so that they can be sued by the government, provide a single entity for taxation, and other transactions that would otherwise be complicated by the fact that dozens, up to thousands, of people make up a corporation. While older than the United States, the specific justification used in the US is that people should not become deprived of rights when they act collectively.<br /> <br /> Corporations, however, are not covered by the Fifth Amendment, or indeed, most other legislation pertaining to the individual; a shareholder is not protected against self-incrimination if he or she may be called testify against the corporation they own a share in. They also have no right to privacy, and their right to free speech is currently on shaky ground as the Citizens United ruling made no actual mention of corporate personhood or any involvement of the Fourteenth Amendment, which is the closest thing to a guarantee of civil rights in the Constitution at present. So legally they are not completely people, and there's no universe where a court would actually entertain the idea that, Iunno, corporations ought to be free from discrimination in housing or free from slavery for the simple fact that these circumstances are not relevant concerns to a corporation. They're people in that you can tax them or sue them like any other person. In no other way do they possess rights, no more than any other licensed business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>A Green Sun Destrier</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/77-kongurous","name":"kongurous","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar77_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"417"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}